{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>עד.</b> The meaning is: and the light — this is the light of dawn that rises before the sun shines, and it stands after its coming for a third of one of the equal hours." "And after he mentioned the sun, what need was there to mention the light and the moon and the stars? Because there are created beings, such as birds, that cannot fly by day because of the glare of the sun's light. But the nearer [explanation] is that this is the way of Scripture to precede or to delay, as (Psalms 121:4) — behold he neither slumbers nor sleeps, and slumber is lighter than sleep." "There are interpreters [who say] ושבו העבים — concerning weeping. And others said: concerning the moisture that overpowers him. But the correct view in my eyes is its plain sense, for the sick person at the time of his death — the world darkens for him, and it appears to him as though the clouds have hidden the light. And so it is: ושבו העבים — to thicken after the rain."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "Resolved המקר' as an abbreviation of המקרא (Scripture); the apostrophe indicates a supralinear abbreviation marker in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:18.203241452Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}